    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`pad_mm_token_pairs` in `python/sglang/srt/managers/mm_utils.py` is typed to accept `data_token_pairs: Optional[List[Tuple[int, int]]] = None` and includes a fallback to `mm_inputs.im_start_id` / `mm_inputs.im_end_id` (or logging a warning and returning `input_ids` unchanged when no token pairs are available, e.g., when called with `token_pairs or None` from `dots3_common`). However, three bugs prevented the `None` fallback from ever working:\n\n1. Line 267 executed `[s for s, _e in data_token_pairs]` **before** checking `if data_token_pairs is None:`, immediately raising `TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not iterable`.\n2. Line 271 set `data_token_pairs = [mm_inputs.im_start_id, mm_inputs.im_end_id]` (a flat list of 2 ints rather than a list of `(start, end)` 2-tuples `[(mm_inputs.im_start_id, mm_inputs.im_end_id)]`), which both shadowed the subsequent `if data_token_pairs is None:` check when `im_start_id` was `None` and raised `TypeError: cannot unpack non-iterable int object` when `im_start_id` / `im_end_id` were set.\n3. `MultiModalityDataPaddingPatternTokenPairs.__init__` similarly iterated over `data_token_pairs` without guarding for `None`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Resolve the `data_token_pairs is None` fallback first, constructing `[(mm_inputs.im_start_id, mm_inputs.im_end_id)]` only when both `mm_inputs.im_start_id` and `mm_inputs.im_end_id` are non-`None`.\n- Compute `data_start_token_ids` after the `data_token_pairs is None` early return.\n- Guard `data_token_pairs or []` in `MultiModalityDataPaddingPatternTokenPairs.__init__`.\n- Add unit tests in `test/registered/unit/managers/test_mm_pad_token_pairs.py`.\n\n## Acknowledgements\n\nCredit to @mickqian (#44845, #6187) and @JustinTong0323 (#7629) for the multimodal token padding helpers in `mm_utils.py`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format Guide](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-your-code).\n- [x] Add unit tests as outlined in the [Running Unit Tests Guide](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#running-unit-tests-and-adding-new-tests).\n- [x] Update documentation / docstrings as needed.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #40730454457](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40730454457)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #40730454337](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40730454337)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #40730454368](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40730454368)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
